      "id": "18317",
      "key": "SFCC-191",
      "summary": "Promo Code Entry & Validation",
      "description": "As a \nShopper, \nI want\n to enter a promotional code on the cart page and receive immediate feedback on whether it is valid, \nso that\n I can apply eligible discounts to my order before proceeding to checkout.\nThe promo code entry field is visible and editable on the cart/bag page. Multiple promo codes may be entered sequentially per the current design. This story covers the entry mechanism, validation feedback, and Remove interaction only — display of discount lines and saving amounts in the order summary is covered in another story. Auto-applied discounts (e.g. customer group discounts such as Gold VIC) are displayed in the same discounts area — their rendering is handled in SFCC-38 and SFCC-42. For international (Global-e) checkouts, coupon validation occurs in SFCC before cart handoff — Global-e does not re-validate. Promotion calculations execute in the customer's selected ship-to currency. Promo codes and discount values must be included in the Global-e cart payload — see PRC-43/PRC-46 and the broader Global-e cart handoff story.",
