      "id": "18195",
      "key": "SFCC-113",
      "summary": "Search Page UI – Empty State & Autocomplete",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper, \nI want \na responsive search page experience when I open and interact with the search bar, \nso that\n I can quickly find products or navigate to relevant categories whether I'm still deciding what to search or actively typing a query.\nThis story covers the full PWA build of the search page across two states:\nEmpty/focused state\n — triggered when the shopper clicks the search input and the dedicated search page opens before any text has been entered. The search input renders with placeholder copy \"What are you looking for?\" and a greyed-out, non-clickable Search button. A product grid is displayed below (currently designed as New Arrivals tiles with no price — see open items).\nTyped/autocomplete state\n — triggered as soon as the shopper begins typing. Keyword suggestions appear below the search input, and the product grid updates depending on whether the term matches catalogue items (labelled \"Recommended for You\" or \"New Arrivals\" — see open items). Product tiles show image, name, and price (price display to be confirmed — see open items). Selecting a suggestion or pressing Enter submits the search and navigates to the results page.\nThe search input in the nav displays the placeholder text \"SEARCH\" on desktop and a search icon on mobile. Clicking it from any page opens the dedicated search page — this is not an inline dropdown or overlay anchored to the nav bar.\nDepends on SFCC-112 (Recommendations – Einstein Configuration & Zone Setup) — Einstein must be provisioned before the search page can be built and tested against live data.\nEmpty State:\nAutocomplete - New arrivals no price\nAutocomplete - Recommended for you - price",
